<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Magnus VI of Norway</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1238–1280</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Magnus the Lawmender, Magnus Lagabøte</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Magnus VI, called the Lawmender, was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> from 1263 to 1280. He gave Norway a single national law code, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnus-lagabotes-land-law">Landslov of 1274</a>, and a town law in 1276, replacing the regional laws. By the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-perth">Treaty of Perth</a> in 1266 he ceded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrides">Hebrides</a> and the Isle of Man to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> while keeping <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkney">Orkney</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shetland">Shetland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/magnus-vi-of-norway.jpg" alt="Magnus VI of Norway" width="197" height="277" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexander Bugge (1870–1929) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Magnus_Haakonsson_(Stavanger_cathedral).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
